findings.detail:
`saveRecordEditor` (src/routes/roster/+page.svelte:1152). Idiom to copy, lines 1183-1186:
```
if (recordForm.name.trim() === '') {
	recordSaveError = { memberId, kind: 'name-required' };
	return;
}
```
This sits after the single-flight/lookup/error-reset preamble (lines 1157-1173: `recordSavingMemberId !== null` early-return, cfg/lookup guards, `recordSaveError = null`, `recordStatus = ''`) and immediately BEFORE `const g = routeLoad.generation;` (1187) and `recordSavingMemberId = memberId;` (1188) — i.e. before the in-flight guard is armed. The fresh `loadMemberRecord` re-read await is further down at line 1201, inside the try block, gated behind `recordSavingMemberId = memberId`. Per #268 review F2's comment (1174-1182), the reason this all lives in the handler rather than `required`/native validation is stated explicitly: the editor is a `<div>` not a `<form>`, save is `type="button"` + onclick, so browser constraint validation never runs automatically here — Gama's comment 1 in #283 confirms the same for `type="email"`.
The phone and email guards must slot in the SAME spot as name-required — after line 1186's `return}` and before line 1187 — so they run before `recordSavingMemberId` is set and before the fresh-lookup suspension point, exactly as the task specifies.
